``` SR-02 | Skipped Scheduled Searches and Why
    Splunk Administrator Field Manual - Gaurav Malik

    Use case: Alerts did not fire and reports are missing runs; list every
    skipped scheduled search with its skip reason, owning app, and skip ratio.
    Run on: SH. In an SHC, host shows which member the captain assigned the
    job to.
    Query: Main query
    If this returns nothing, run probes/SR-02-probe.spl to confirm the data it
    reads exists here.
```
index=_internal sourcetype=scheduler earliest=-24h
    (status=success OR status=skipped OR status=continued OR status=deferred)
| eval skipped=if(status="skipped", 1, 0)
| stats count as attempts sum(skipped) as skipped
        values(eval(if(status="skipped", reason, null()))) as skip_reasons
        by host app savedsearch_name user
| where skipped > 0
| eval skip_pct=round(100 * skipped / attempts, 1)
| sort - skipped
| table host app savedsearch_name user attempts skipped skip_pct skip_reasons
